        "content": "<p>Takashiidobe opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14694\">issue #14694</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<h3><code>.clif</code> Test Case</h3>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"n\">missing_division</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">i8</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"n\">block0</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">i8</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nc\">v1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iconst</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kt\">i8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">v10</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sdiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iconst</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kt\">i8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v2</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h3>Steps to Reproduce</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>compile on any architecture</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Expected Results</h3>\n<p>the sdiv cannot trap and is dead, so i would expect something like return 0</p>\n<h3>Actual Results</h3>\n<p>for x86_64 I see:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"GAS\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nf\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rbp</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">mov</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rbp</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rsp</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">mov</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rax</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rdi</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">cbw</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">mov</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">esi</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">7</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">idiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">sil</span><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">; trap: int_ovf</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">xor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">eax</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">eax</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">mov</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rsp</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rbp</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">pop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rbp</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">ret</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>with the trap comment so I assume it's not properly deleted</p>\n<h3>Versions and Environment</h3>\n<p>Cranelift version or commit: 0.136.2</p>\n<p>Operating system: linux</p>\n<p>Architecture: x86_64, though this happens on all architectures since this isn't lowering specific</p>\n<h3>Extra Info</h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/5908\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/5908</a> seems to indicate that work was done to handle this problem already.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://clif-explorer.takashiidobe.com/#code=ZnVuY3Rpb24gJW1pc3NpbmdfZGl2aXNpb24oaTMyKSAtPiBpMzIgewpibG9jazAodjA6IGkzMik6CiAgICB2MSA9IGljb25zdC5pMzIgNwogICAgdjEwID0gc2RpdiB2MCwgdjEgIAogICAgdjIgPSBpY29uc3QuaTMyIDAKICAgIHJldHVybiB2MiAgCn0&amp;version=0.136.2&amp;arch=x86_64&amp;tab=asm&amp;flags=opt_level=speed&amp;fn=%25missing_division&amp;args=%5B%22%22,%222%22%5D\">i32</a> and i64 already properly handle this case, <a href=\"https://clif-explorer.takashiidobe.com/#code=ZnVuY3Rpb24gJW1pc3NpbmdfZGl2aXNpb24oaTgpIC0-IGk4IHsKYmxvY2swKHYwOiBpOCk6CiAgICB2MSA9IGljb25zdC5pOCA3CiAgICB2MTAgPSBzZGl2IHYwLCB2MSAgCiAgICB2MiA9IGljb25zdC5pOCAwCiAgICByZXR1cm4gdjIgIAp9&amp;version=0.136.2&amp;arch=x86_64&amp;tab=asm&amp;flags=opt_level=speed&amp;fn=%25missing_division&amp;args=%5B%22%22,%222%22%5D\">i8</a> and i16 do not. </p>\n<p>I'm assuming that just extending i8 and i16 to i32 is a cheap fix for this particular problem, since they both just emit, which deletes the division entirely</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"GAS\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nf\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rbp</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">mov</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rbp</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rsp</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">xor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">eax</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">eax</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">mov</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rsp</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rbp</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">pop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"no\">rbp</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">ret</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</blockquote>",
